<title>USA: USA-STOCKS-OPEN.</title>
<headline>USA-STOCKS-OPEN.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Wall Street stocks weakened with bonds at the start of trading on Monday as an atmosphere of caution permeated the market ahead of Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan's Humphrey-Hawkins testimony this week.</p>
<p>The Dow Jones industrial average was off 23 at 6,909, while the Nasdaq Composite was down seven at 1,327 and the S&amp;P Index off two at 799.</p>
<p>The 30-year long bond was off 13/32 to yield 6.67 percent.</p>
